  <div id="sutta">
  
    <h4 id="thag1.10" class="h1">Thag 1:10  Puṇṇamāsa</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>Whoever,</p>
              <p class="v2">a master of knowing,</p>
              <p class="v2">contented,<span class="fn"><a href="#thag1.10note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
              <p class="v2">restrained in mind,</p>
              <p>destroys longing for here &amp; beyond,</p>
              <p>unsmeared with regard to all dhammas,</p>
              <p>would know the arising-&amp;-disbanding</p>
              <p class="v2">of the world.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-->
            <div class="note">
              <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
              <p id="thag1.10note01">1. Reading <em>santusito</em> with the Thai edition. Other editions have <em>samito</em>—calmed, appeased—which doesn’t fit the meter.</p>
            </div><!--end notes-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
